          <p>
            Two caveats on the Gold Standard column. Other grocery listings still show an older Gold Standard panel with a 30.4 g scoop and 50 mg of sodium, so the sodium figure in particular depends on which lot you get. And Optimum Nutrition lists 24 flavors on its US site; only Double Rich Chocolate and Vanilla Ice Cream appeared in the NSF Certified for Sport database when we checked on 19 November 2026.
          </p>

          <p>
            Protein density, the share of each scoop that is protein, is the quickest way to see how much filler a powder carries. Isopure Zero Carb is 81% protein by weight and Gold Standard is 77%, which is the measurable difference between a pure isolate and an isolate-led blend. Isopure Low Carb drops to 76% because the chocolate flavor adds cocoa. Our full <a href="/protein-powder-comparison/">protein powder comparison</a> table lists the same figure for every powder we track.
