            Label figures and prices come from our product database, checked against these listings: the <a href="https://www.target.com/p/optimum-nutrition-gold-standard-100-whey-protien-double-chocolate-3-89lbs/-/A-89319296" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Target listing</a> for Gold Standard 100% Whey, the <a href="https://www.optimumnutrition.com/en-us/products/gold-standard-100-whey-protein-powder" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Optimum Nutrition product page</a>, the <a href="https://www.vitacost.com/products/isopure-zero-carb-protein-powder-creamy-vanilla-3-lb-1-36-kg-11460" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Vitacost listing</a> for Isopure Zero Carb, the <a href="https://www.vitacost.com/products/isopure-low-carb-protein-powder-dutch-chocolate-2-98-lb-1-35-kg-14657" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Vitacost listing for Isopure Low Carb</a> and the <a href="https://www.theisopurecompany.com/products/clear-protein-powder" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Isopure Clear Protein page</a>. Certification was checked in the <a href="https://www.nsfsport.com/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">NSF Certified for Sport database</a>.
          </p>

          <p>
            We did not taste or lab-test these powders. Label Scores and cost per 25 g are calculated as described on our <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> page and in <a href="/how-we-test/">how we test</a>. If a label has changed since we checked, the tub in your hand is the source to trust.
